---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import InfoPage from '../components/InfoPage.astro';
// Every fact is Stillpool's own: the three nbl: keys (settings.ts and boot.js, progress/store.ts, Map.astro), the save code
// (progress/code.ts, SaveCode.astro), read aloud (readaloud.ts) and the count (analytics.ts). The count's paragraphs show only
// in a build that has it, as on /help/. Rights and the regulator follow the NeuroBridgeEDU privacy page.
const count = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ANALYTICS === '1';
const toc = [
  { id: 'summary', title: 'In short' },
  { id: 'stored', title: 'What is stored on your device' },
  { id: 'received', title: 'What the host receives' },
  { id: 'lab', title: 'The practice lab' },
  { id: 'feedback', title: 'Feedback' },
  ...(count ? [{ id: 'count', title: 'Counting visits' }] : []),
  { id: 'cookies', title: 'Cookies and why there is no banner' },
  { id: 'use', title: 'How this information is used' },
  { id: 'choices', title: 'Your choices' },
  { id: 'rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact' },
];
---

<Base title="Privacy notice" description="The privacy notice for Stillpool, the free AI lessons by NeuroBridgeEDU." wide>
  <InfoPage title="Privacy notice" {toc} updated="10 October 2026">
    <p slot="intro" class="lede">
      This notice describes Stillpool at learn.neurobridgeedu.eu. Stillpool has no accounts and sets no cookies. What it keeps on your device is
      only what you asked it to keep: your progress and your settings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="summary">In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There are no accounts and no cookies.</li>
      <li>Your settings, progress and map choices are kept in this browser and are not sent anywhere.</li>
      <li>Loading a page or a recording is a request to this site, which is hosted by Vercel.</li>
      <li>The lessons do not call an AI service. The practice lab does, only when you press Send.</li>
      <li>A message you send on the feedback page is saved on a server in the EU. Nothing is sent until you press Send feedback.</li>
      {count && <li>A cookieless Vercel count records visits to pages. See "Counting visits".</li>}
    </ul>

    <h2 id="stored">What is stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Stillpool uses local storage, the browser's own storage for one site. It is not a cookie and is never sent with a request. It holds three
      items, all kept until you remove them or clear this site's data in your browser:
    </p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Settings</dt>
      <dd>
        Font, text size, spacing, colours, motion, reading ruler, the other reading choices, the reading voice, the reading speed and whether lessons show Simple or
        Deep. Stored as <code>nbl:settings</code>.
      </dd>
      <dt>Progress</dt>
      <dd>
        The lessons you finished, the badges you earned and the activity steps you completed. Stored as <code>nbl:progress</code>. If your browser
        blocks or fills its storage, progress may not be kept.
      </dd>
      <dt>Map choices</dt>
      <dd>Which topics you opened on the lesson map. Stored as <code>nbl:topics</code>.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>
      The save code and its QR code hold your finished lessons and badges, and nothing else: not your settings, map choices or activity steps. They
      are made on your device and go nowhere unless you share them. Anyone who has your code can see which lessons you finished. A restore link
      carries the code after a <code>#</code> in the address, the part a browser does not send to a server, and Stillpool removes it from the
      address once it has used it. Restoring adds to the progress already in the browser; it does not erase it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="received">What the host receives</h2>
    <p>
      Opening a page, or playing a recording, asks this site's server for files. Stillpool is hosted by Vercel, which receives ordinary request
      information such as your IP address and browser details, and keeps server logs. Read
      <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Vercel's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read aloud uses Emma, a computer voice recorded in advance and hosted on this site. Where a recording is missing, it uses a voice already on
      your device. Only voices that run on the device are offered, so the lesson's words are not sent to a speech service.
    </p>
    <h2 id="lab">The practice lab</h2>
    <p>
      The practice lab at <a href="/lab/">/lab/</a> is the one place on Stillpool that uses an AI service. It is optional, and nothing is sent until you
      open it and press Send. When you do, the text you typed in the lab is sent to Mistral AI, a company in Paris, which writes the reply.
    </p>
    <p>
      The text goes through this site's server, so Vercel and Mistral process it to answer you. Stillpool keeps no copy, stores nothing on your device
      and logs no text. This notice says nothing about what Mistral keeps. Read
      <a href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Mistral's privacy policy</a>, and leave out names and other personal
      details.
    </p>
    <h2 id="feedback">Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      The feedback page at <a href="/feedback/">/feedback/</a> is optional, and nothing is sent until you press Send feedback. When you do, what is
      sent is your message and what it is about: the whole site, the practice lab or one lesson.
    </p>
    <p>
      The message goes to this site's server, then to a workflow tool run by NeuroBridgeEDU on its own server in the EU. There it is saved in a
      table that the makers read. Stillpool asks for no name and no account, and does not store the message on your device. The host's usual logs
      apply, as for any request.
    </p>
    <p>
      To ask for a message to be removed, write to <a href="mailto:contact@neurobridgeedu.eu">contact@neurobridgeedu.eu</a> and quote its text.
      Please do not write your name, your email or anything private in a message.
    </p>
    {
      count && (
        <>
          <h2 id="count">Counting visits</h2>
          <p>
            Stillpool counts how many times its pages are opened, so its makers can see if anyone uses it. Vercel, the company that hosts this
            site, does the counting with Vercel Web Analytics.
          </p>
          <p>When a page opens, the count records:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>the page address</li>
            <li>the site that linked here</li>
            <li>the time</li>
            <li>the country, and the region and city where they are known</li>
            <li>the kind of device, with its system and browser, and their versions</li>
            <li>the version of the counting script</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            It does not use cookies. It tells visits apart with a code made from the request, and Vercel resets
            that code every day. It does not follow you across sites or build a profile of you. The data is used for combined totals only.
          </p>
          <p>
            A page opened with a save code, or any other text after its address, is not counted. Your answers, settings, progress and save code
            are not sent to the count. Read
            <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">how Vercel describes this count</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and why there is no banner</h2>
    <p>
      A cookie is a small file a site asks your browser to keep and send back on every request. Stillpool sets none. A cookie banner asks for
      consent to store things that are not needed. Here the only things stored on your device are the progress and settings you asked for{
        count ? ', and the count sets no cookie' : ''
      }, so there is nothing to consent to.
    </p>

    <h2 id="use">How this information is used</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Settings change how lessons look and read to you.</li>
      <li>Progress shows your finished lessons and badges.</li>
      <li>Map choices keep your topics open or closed as you left them.</li>
      <li>Text you send from the practice lab is used to write the reply to you.</li>
      <li>A message you send as feedback is saved and read by the makers, to improve the site.</li>
      <li>The host serves the site and keeps logs to run it{count ? '; the count shows how often pages are visited' : ''}.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      In Settings, Delete my progress removes finished lessons, badges and steps from this browser. It leaves your settings and map choices. To
      remove all three, clear this site's data in your browser. A save code you kept can bring your progress back, so delete the code too if you
      do not want that.
    </p>

    <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the European law on personal data, you may ask what is held about you, ask for it to be
      corrected or erased, object to its use and ask for a copy. Stillpool has no accounts, so the only personal data it can see is what the
      host's logs hold, any email you send and any text you send from the practice lab, which it does not keep. A feedback message is kept: see "Feedback". You may complain to the Irish Data Protection Commission at
      <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" rel="noopener">dataprotection.ie</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href="mailto:contact@neurobridgeedu.eu">contact@neurobridgeedu.eu</a> and put "Privacy" in the subject. Please do not email a
      save code.
    </p>
  </InfoPage>
</Base>
